fields.InputDefinition:
{
  "goal": "Open the 'People' entity via the LEFT sidebar 'Search record types...' box (type 'People', click the exact match; or navigate to http://localhost:4200/app/data-explorer/Data?entity=MJ_BizApps_Common:%20People), type 'Rodriguez' in the grid's filter box, click the Elena Rodriguez row, then click 'Open Full Record' to load the full form. This shared setup is done ONCE. This form uses a LEFT section rail (Details and the related sections such as Contact Methods and Relationships, possibly with a 'More' folder at the bottom); the section and layout controls live in the toolbar's 'View' panel (the 'View' button at the TOP-RIGHT of the toolbar, sliders icon) — open it when a step needs it, and reopen it if it has closed. Then exercise these form controls IN ORDER, and as you finish each set \"checkpointReached\" to the exact checkpoint name shown: (1) section-search — in the View panel's 'Search sections...' input type a term matching a section name (e.g. 'Contact') and confirm the left rail narrows to the matching sections, then type gibberish (e.g. 'zzzqqq') and confirm a 'No sections found' empty state with a 'Clear search' action, then click 'Clear search' (or the × in the search box) so every section returns; (2) section-nav — in the left rail click a section other than the current one (e.g. 'Contact Methods' or 'Relationships') and confirm the form body switches to that section's content and the rail highlights it, then click 'Details' to return; (3) width-toggle — in the View panel click 'Use full width' (or 'Center content' when already full width) and confirm the form content layout width visibly changes; (4) section-manager — in the View panel click 'Reorder sections' (bars-staggered icon) and confirm the 'Manage Sections' drawer opens listing sections with up/down arrows and a 'Reset to defaults' button, then close it with its × button; (5) section-rail-toggle — click the rail's 'Hide sections' button (double chevron « at the top of the rail, next to the pin icon) and confirm the rail collapses to a narrow vertical tab labeled with the current section, then click that tab (tooltip 'Show sections — <section>') and confirm the full rail returns. Keep going until every control has been exercised. Pages can take 10-30s to load in this resource-constrained environment — wait for content rather than navigating away.",
  "startUrl": "http://localhost:4200",
  "allowedDomains": [
    "localhost",
    "*.auth0.com"
  ],
  "auth": {
    "bindings": [
      {
        "domains": [
          "localhost",
          "*.auth0.com"
        ],
        "method": {
          "Type": "Basic",
          "Username": "{{authUsername}}",
          "Password": "{{authPassword}}",
          "Strategy": "FormLogin"
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}

fields.ExpectedOutcomes:
{
  "goalCompleted": true,
  "finalUrlPattern": "^http://localhost:4200",
  "minConfidence": 0.7,
  "maxSteps": 65,
  "checkpoints": [
    {
      "name": "section-search",
      "instruction": "section search narrows the rail and shows no-match empty state",
      "visualCriteria": [
        "Typing a matching term in the View panel's 'Search sections...' box narrows the left section rail to matching sections, and typing a non-matching term shows a 'No sections found' empty state with a 'Clear search' option"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "section-nav",
      "instruction": "left section rail switches the form body",
      "visualCriteria": [
        "Clicking a different section in the form's left section rail (e.g. Contact Methods) switches the form body to that section's content and highlights that item in the rail"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "width-toggle",
      "instruction": "form width toggle changes content width",
      "visualCriteria": [
        "Clicking the View panel's width toggle (Use full width / Center content) visibly changes the form content layout width — the content widens to full width or re-centers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "section-manager",
      "instruction": "Manage Sections drawer opens with reorder controls",
      "visualCriteria": [
        "Clicking 'Reorder sections' in the View panel opens a 'Manage Sections' drawer listing the form's sections with up/down move buttons and a 'Reset to defaults' button"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "section-rail-toggle",
      "instruction": "hide then show the section rail",
      "visualCriteria": [
        "Clicking 'Hide sections' collapses the left section rail to a narrow vertical tab labeled with the current section, and clicking that tab restores the full rail"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
